# UI theme (GEAR look)

When editing menus, overlays, sheets, or dialogs under `lib/ui/`:

1. Follow **`docs/UI_THEME.md`** (reference = GEAR inventory sheet).
2. Prefer **`MenuChrome`** + **`GameTheme`** primitives — do not invent new colors/radii.
3. Titles → `GameTheme.menuTitle`; sections → `MenuChrome.sectionLabel`; lists → `cardBox` / `listCard`.
4. Multi-tab overlays → `MenuChrome.tabRail` (same as GEAR/BAG/TOOLS).
5. Actions → `KenneyButton` (brown / grey / red). No Material `TextButton` in forge dialogs.
6. Press Start (`GameTheme.pixel`) only for combat HUD and tiny tags — not menu titles.
7. Skip restyling: combat HUD, bottom nav, start menu, item tooltips, hub world-path scene.

English in-game copy. If you add a new shared chrome helper, put it on `MenuChrome` and mention it in `docs/UI_THEME.md`.
